b102-array-sort-correct-callbacks does not compile: the engine rejects all three comparators the fixture calls correct, and the LSP is silent on every one

Found by lane-resolver while building B145's engine-verdict corpus, measured live
against Openplanet 1.29.14. This is not a corpus bookkeeping detail — it is a
false negative in the checker, and the fixture's own name asserts the opposite.

WHAT WAS MEASURED
  tests/fixtures/issue-repros/b102-array-sort-correct-callbacks/
  Engine verdict: REJECTED. All three comparators the fixture labels "correct"
  fail to compile in the real engine.
  LSP verdict: silent on all three. Zero diagnostics.

So the fixture is misnamed, AND we agree with a spelling the engine refuses.
B145's corpus is what made this visible: nothing else in the suite compares our
verdict against the engine's on this fixture, and a fixture asserting "no
diagnostics expected" passes forever whether or not the code is legal.

WHY THIS IS B144's FAMILY
  B145's ticket called this pair B144's natural first entry, and it is. B144 was
  the checker demanding a spelling the engine rejects (Json::Value@ const parsed
  as a Named type equal to nothing). This is the mirror: the checker ACCEPTING a
  spelling the engine rejects. Same seam — the array-sort / Less callback
  binding — opposite polarity.

  Whoever takes this must establish the engine's actual rule for a sort
  comparator's parameter binding before changing anything, from the engine's own
  messages, not from what the fixture assumed. Do not fix the fixture to match
  the checker. Do not fix the checker to match the fixture. Get the engine's
  answer first and let it decide which of the two is wrong — quite possibly both.

RISK POLARITY
  Making this diagnose ADDS errors to real plugins, same inverted polarity as
  B152. A fleet sweep with EXPOSURE reported is mandatory: a zero-difference
  sweep proves nothing here unless it also reports how many plugins contain a
  sort callback at all. See docs/verification-hazards.md, "Design the instrument
  to report EXPOSURE, or a zero is uninterpretable".

DEPENDS ON B145 being merged (the corpus and its verdict column are the
evidence). Assign to lane-const, which owns the B144/B152 const-exactness seam.